  "markdown": "## Overview\nCostco Wholesale Corp. operates membership warehouses and e-commerce sites based on a low-price, high-volume model [10-K line 00134]. The company leverages volume purchasing, efficient distribution, and reduced handling to operate profitably at lower gross margins than most other retailers [10-K line 00134]. As of August 30, 2026, it operates in over 20 countries with a total of 939 warehouses [release line 00021].\n\n## Market Positioning and Growth Outlook\nCostco competes globally with various types of retailers including supermarkets, supercenters, online retailers, and other warehouse clubs like Sam’s Club and BJ’s Wholesale Club [10-K line 00190]. Its competitive advantages include its membership format, which reinforces member loyalty and provides continuing fee revenue, and its pricing authority, perceived by members as consistently offering the most competitive values [10-K line 00398]. Additionally, Costco's private-label brand, Kirkland Signature, is noted for being high quality and offered at prices generally lower than national brands [10-K line 00192].\n\nCostco’s growth is driven by increasing net sales, particularly comparable sales, achieved through increased shopping frequency and average ticket size [10-K line 00398]. Opening new warehouses also contributes to net sales growth; in 2026, the company opened 28 new warehouses [release line 00014]. The company's ability to maintain high membership renewal rates and increase penetration of Executive memberships supports profitability [10-K line 00406]. Additionally, its e-commerce operations and digitally-enabled sales are growing significantly, representing 11% of total net sales in 2026 [10-K line 00153].\n\n## Future Developments and Strategic Recommendations\nSeveral catalysts support Costco’s continued performance. One significant catalyst is the ongoing expansion of membership fee revenue, driven by new member sign-ups, fee increases, and upgrades to Executive memberships [10-K line 00456]. Another key catalyst is the company's strong focus on employee retention and development, which contributes to high productivity and low turnover rates [10-K line 00181]. Furthermore, the company's strategic investments in technology and digital platforms enhance member convenience and broaden product offerings [10-K line 00153].\n\nIn addition, future developments are likely to center around continued international expansion, leveraging the membership model to penetrate new markets and increase penetration within existing ones. Strategic recommendations include maintaining focus on operational excellence, optimizing supply chain efficiency, and enhancing digital experiences to meet evolving consumer expectations.\n\nCostco's recent performance highlights strong financials, with net income increasing by 14% to $9.226 billion in 2026 [release line 00020]. The company also opened 28 new warehouses, including three relocations, for a total of 25 net new warehouses in the U.S., Canada, and Other International segments [10-K line 00415]. Moreover, the Board of Directors approved a 13% increase in the quarterly cash dividend [10-K line 00423]. The company received IEEPA tariff refunds totaling $184 million in 2026, with $174 million recorded as a reduction to merchandise costs and $10 million as interest income [10-K line 00426].",
